1,null,3,"e/ef/Andrea_del_Verrocchio_-_Crocifissione.jpg/330px-Andrea_del_Verrocchio_-_Crocifissione.jpg",3,16,1,0,35,"Crucifixion avec saint Jérôme et saint Antoine abbé",null,null,null,51],[141757437,"Mary with the Child",1450,0,1,null,3,"d/df/1468_Verrocchio_Maria_mit_dem_Kind_Gem%C3%A4ldegalerie_Berlin_anagoria.jpg/330px-1468_Verrocchio_Maria_mit_dem_Kind_Gem%C3%A4ldegalerie_Berlin_anagoria.jpg",3,1,1,0,11,"La Vierge et l'Enfant",null,null,null,51]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":2,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"473237":["The equestrian statue of Bartolomeo Colleoni is a Renaissance sculpture in Campo Santi Giovanni e Paolo, Venice, Italy, created by Andrea del Verrocchio in 1480–1488. Portraying the condottiero Bartolomeo Colleoni, it has a height of 395 cm excluding the pedestal.","Equestrian statue of Bartolomeo Colleoni (Venice)"],"917483":["The Loggia del Mercato Nuovo, popularly known as the Loggia del Porcellino, is a building in Florence, Italy. It is so called to distinguish it from the Mercato vecchio that used to be located in the area of today's Piazza della Repubblica.","Loggia del Mercato Nuovo"],"1059211":["The Baptism of Christ is an oil-on-panel painting finished around 1475 in the studio of the Italian Renaissance painter Andrea del Verrocchio and generally ascribed to him and his pupil Leonardo da Vinci.","The Baptism of Christ (Verrocchio and Leonardo)"],"2415504":["David is a bronze statue by the Italian Renaissance artist Andrea del Verrocchio. It was most likely made between 1473 and 1475.","David (Verrocchio)"],"2902596":["Christ and Saint Thomas (1467–1483) is a bronze statue by Andrea del Verrocchio made for one of the fourteen niches on the exterior walls of the Orsanmichele in Florence, Italy. It is now replaced in that location by a cast and the original has been moved inside the building, which is now a museum.","Christ and Saint Thomas (Verrocchio)"],"3701200":["Woman with Flowers is a marble sculpture 60 centimetres (24 in) in height executed by Andrea del Verrocchio between 1475 and 1480. It is in the Bargello Museum in Florence.","Dama col mazzolino"],"3842620":["The Virgin and Child with Two Angels is a painting by the Italian Renaissance painter Andrea del Verrocchio, dating from circa 1467–1469. It is in the National Gallery, London, United Kingdom.","Virgin and Child with Two Angels (Verrocchio)"],"3842726":["The Piazza Madonna is a tempera on panel painting, dating to 1474-1486 and held in Pistoia Cathedral.","Piazza Madonna"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}